  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It's always been requested to allow world authors to force hiding name tags. This has come with concerns about security, etc.\n\nI suggest an alternative solution, whereby map authors can set their world to default name tags off, however people can freely turn them back on. The catch, is that anyone who turns on their nametags, will also have their own nametag turned on only for them. Meaning, everyone else will see the nametag of anyone who has nametags turned on.\n\nThis way, whatever security, etc, reasons impede on allowing nametags to be forced off, is avoided because at anytime someone can turn their nametags back on. But doing so makes it that everyone else who has nametags off, will see that one persons nametag, which will allow the players to tell if anyone is trying to cheat, and it would make it that attempting to cheat that way, would only make yourself visible as well.",
